WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:07.360
Blackbeard, Akainu, Shanks. Who will be the final&nbsp;
boss of One Piece? Oda-Sensei has treated us to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.360 --> 00:00:13.280
some perfectly punchable villains throughout&nbsp;
One Piece, but as we near the final saga,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:18.880
we can probably count the major enemies&nbsp;
that Luffy will beat down on one hand.

00:00:18.880 --> 00:00:24.640
So today we’ll explore who we most want to see&nbsp;
Luffy go toe-to-toe with as we wonder - will we&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:31.680
ever get a punch as satisfying as the one where&nbsp;
he knocked the color right out of St. Charloss?

00:00:31.680 --> 00:00:38.640
The two foes at the top of everyone’s lists&nbsp;
are Akainu and Blackbeard. What makes them the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.640 --> 00:00:42.320
perfect final opponents for&nbsp;
Luffy is that both Blackbeard&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:42.320 --> 00:00:48.320
and Akainu are the perfect representatives&nbsp;
of their factions in the One Piece world.

00:00:48.320 --> 00:00:52.960
Oh, and massive shoutout to Blackbird&nbsp;
&amp; Skyberry, my two subscribers of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:56.400
day. Thanks for hitting subscribe for new&nbsp;
content and helping me raise my bounty.

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:04.160
Akainu is the quintessential marine - As the&nbsp;
fleet admiral, he represents everything that this&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:09.920
organization stands for, and is the de&nbsp;
facto leader - ignoring (as he sometimes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:15.600
does) the Gorosei. He is a believer in&nbsp;
absolute justice. In Sakazuki’s eyes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:22.880
no crime should go unpunished. All pirates&nbsp;
are criminals and he is the appointed judge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.880 --> 00:01:27.920
jury, and executioner - as much as Enies&nbsp;
Lobby would like to have a say in that.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:33.120
Even if he disagrees with the Gorosei&nbsp;
or Celestial Dragons, he will do&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.120 --> 00:01:38.880
everything in his power to uphold the order that&nbsp;
the World Government represents. According to him&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:44.560
a world must be founded on rules and authority.&nbsp;
Without submitting to this ordered hierarchy,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:50.080
the world will descend into anarchy and&nbsp;
chaos - a chaos that the world of piracy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:50.080 --> 00:01:56.480
embodies. This doesn’t extend only to pirates&nbsp;
that inflict violence upon innocent people;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.320 --> 00:02:04.400
even the carefree adventuring that the Straw&nbsp;
Hat crew engages in risks corroding the balance&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:11.520
of society. This makes him a perfect counter to&nbsp;
Luffy, who believes that everyone should be free&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:11.520 --> 00:02:16.800
to choose their own destinies and follow their&nbsp;
dreams - to party, to eat their fill, and to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:23.680
adventure. Akainu would stamp these things out in&nbsp;
service of making a more tightly structured world.

00:02:23.680 --> 00:02:28.800
Our first introduction to Akainu shows&nbsp;
us just how far he’s willing to go in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:34.800
name of Absolute Justice. On the island of&nbsp;
Ohara, he single-handedly killed a ship of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.800
citizens fleeing the Buster Call. None of the&nbsp;
people leaving were the librarians who held the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:47.200
secrets of the poneglyphs. In fact, these evacuees&nbsp;
left Robin to die on the island so that they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:52.240
themselves could escape. However, Akainu felt&nbsp;
that even the smallest chance that someone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:58.160
leaving the island held the librarians’ secrets&nbsp;
posed too great a risk to the World Government.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.160 --> 00:03:05.680
To the horror of even another admiral, Aokiji,&nbsp;
he destroyed the ship along with everyone on it.

00:03:05.680 --> 00:03:10.720
Blackbeard, on the other hand, is a&nbsp;
perfect representative of the world&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.720 --> 00:03:14.560
of piracy. Like Luffy, he is&nbsp;
one of the Yonkou - the Four&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:20.080
Emperors of the New World - and a prime&nbsp;
candidate in the race to find the One Piece.

00:03:20.080 --> 00:03:26.400
If you were to ask someone on the street to name&nbsp;
a pirate, a real life one, chances are they’d&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:32.240
say Blackbeard. Likely, they might not even know&nbsp;
the names of any other famous real-life pirates.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.240 --> 00:03:37.520
They’d probably name Captain Jack Sparrow before&nbsp;
they got to their Anne Bonneys or Francis Drakes.

00:03:37.520 --> 00:03:41.120
Oda gave Marshall D. Teach the&nbsp;
moniker of Blackbeard because he&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.120 --> 00:03:44.080
embodies the classic image of a pirate.

00:03:44.080 --> 00:03:49.520
At least, he’s representative of a certain type&nbsp;
of pirate. In the original Romance Dawn one-shots,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:54.240
before the serialization of One Piece as&nbsp;
we know it, Oda-Sensei actually defined&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:54.240 --> 00:04:00.000
two separate classifications of pirates. Pirates&nbsp;
that are looking for adventure on the high seas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:05.120
like the Straw Hats, were termed Peace-Main&nbsp;
Pirates. Whereas pirates who pillage and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.120 --> 00:04:10.640
plunder were called Morganeers. While&nbsp;
Oda didn’t keep the terminology,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.640 --> 00:04:16.400
we can still see echoes of it in&nbsp;
the different approaches to piracy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:22.560
that different crews take. The Blackbeard&nbsp;
pirates are definitely in the Morganeer camp.

00:04:22.560 --> 00:04:26.800
You might think that we haven’t really seen&nbsp;
them do much in the way of classic “pillaging&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:31.920
and plundering”, but the very first reference&nbsp;
we get to Blackbeard in the series actually&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:37.760
confirms this. On Drum Island, Dalton refers&nbsp;
to Blackbeard ransacking the kingdom. In fact,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:43.440
it was the terrifying power of the Blackbeard&nbsp;
pirates that caused Wapol to flee the country&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:48.560
and take all of the doctors with him, setting us&nbsp;
up for Chopper’s introduction. And let’s just take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.560 --> 00:04:53.920
a minute to once again praise the almighty&nbsp;
Goda’s foreshadowing - because we received&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:59.440
whispers of Blackbeard long before Luffy&nbsp;
and Blackbeard’s chance encounter on Jaya.

00:04:59.440 --> 00:05:03.680
Making their home on Beehive Island, the&nbsp;
Blackbeard pirates are creating their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.680 --> 00:05:09.680
version of a pirate paradise. Lawless&nbsp;
and chaotic, he allows his ten titanic&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:15.680
captains to run wild in the New World as&nbsp;
they amass power by collecting devil fruits.

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:20.560
So, how are both of these characters&nbsp;
the perfect enemies for Luffy?

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:27.200
Both of these central antagonists are counters&nbsp;
to Luffy’s core philosophy. Luffy believes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:32.080
in freedom above all else - freedom to&nbsp;
travel, to eat, to party, to adventure.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.160 --> 00:05:38.960
Akainu and the marines restrict the freedom of&nbsp;
people across the seas of One Piece. While they&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:44.880
may protect people from dangerous, violent&nbsp;
pirates, they also enact exploitative taxes,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:44.880 --> 00:05:50.400
restrict travel, and even run protection&nbsp;
for the slave-holding celestial dragons.

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:57.600
Blackbeard, instead of being opposed to Luffy, is&nbsp;
more like the other side of the same coin. Like&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:57.600 --> 00:06:03.520
Luffy, Teach believes in a kind of freedom, but&nbsp;
it’s a freedom that allows someone to use their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:12.560
own power to infringe on the freedom of another.&nbsp;
While Luffy uses his freedom to uplift others&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:12.560 --> 00:06:18.480
and grant them the same freedoms, Blackbeard&nbsp;
uses his freedom toward his own personal gain.

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:24.560
It’s not just that their philosophies are&nbsp;
diametrically opposed that set Akainu and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:30.320
Blackbeard up as the perfect antagonists for&nbsp;
Luffy. The stakes are personal. These two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:37.760
characters are directly responsible for Ace’s&nbsp;
death - Akainu very literally did kill Ace,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:37.760 --> 00:06:42.880
and to add to Luffy’s personal grudge against&nbsp;
the fleet admiral, he killed Ace while Ace was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:47.200
trying to protect Luffy. However, the war&nbsp;
at Marineford never would have occurred&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:54.960
if it weren’t for the actions of Blackbeard. He&nbsp;
captured Ace and turned him over to the Marines&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:54.960 --> 00:07:00.400
in order to claim his status as a Shichibukai.&nbsp;
This, too, partly falls onto Luffy’s shoulders,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.400 --> 00:07:05.840
because Blackbeard was actually pursuing&nbsp;
Luffy at the time that Ace confronted him.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:05.840 --> 00:07:13.760
Before the end of the series, we need to see&nbsp;
Luffy take his revenge on these powerful foes.

00:07:13.760 --> 00:07:17.680
Another figure that we’ll probably see&nbsp;
Luffy fight before the end of One Piece&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.680 --> 00:07:23.680
is the mysterious Im-Sama. So far little&nbsp;
is known about the secret true ruler of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.680 --> 00:07:27.120
the World Government, given that&nbsp;
they’ve only appeared in a single&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.120 --> 00:07:31.360
chapter of the manga. There’s a lot we&nbsp;
have to learn about this shadowy figure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:31.360 --> 00:07:38.160
but given that they’re the head of the World&nbsp;
Government, they appear to be final boss material.

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:44.960
Luffy has a more personal grudge against Akainu,&nbsp;
but Im is Akainu’s boss’s boss, and the real&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:44.960 --> 00:07:52.160
decision maker behind the Marines. If Luffy&nbsp;
wants to bring freedom to the rest of the world,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:59.680
the only way will be to go through them. We know,&nbsp;
too, that Im-Sama has it out for Luffy, too.

00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:02.960
I mean, we don’t know too much&nbsp;
about Im’s motivations, but&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.960 --> 00:08:08.000
whenever I rip up a picture of someone’s face,&nbsp;
it usually means I don’t like that person much.

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:12.880
We also have a few wild cards, though.&nbsp;
These are figures that Luffy could fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:12.880 --> 00:08:20.080
but we really don’t know yet at this&nbsp;
point. A big one that people theorize about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:20.880 --> 00:08:26.880
is the possibility that Luffy will fight&nbsp;
his childhood hero, Shanks. Based on Shanks’&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:26.880 --> 00:08:32.320
secret connection to the Gorosei, some fans&nbsp;
have speculated that Shanks’ motivations are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.320 --> 00:08:40.640
less than good. Perhaps he will prove a true&nbsp;
rival to Luffy for the throne of Pirate King.

00:08:40.640 --> 00:08:45.600
I just released another video about this&nbsp;
possibility. Because I truly belive that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:47.120 --> 00:08:51.840
Shanks and Luffy WIll clash at&nbsp;
some point very soon in the story.

00:08:51.840 --> 00:08:54.880
Maybe they’ll all just have a&nbsp;
good-spirited Davy Back Fight,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.880 --> 00:08:58.240
leading to the 12th and final Straw Hat…Lucky Roo.

00:09:00.240 --> 00:09:03.600
Then, of course, we have absolutely&nbsp;
wild predictions. As we know,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:03.600 --> 00:09:09.200
Oda-sensei is famous for his ridiculous&nbsp;
left turns and unpredictability. So, who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:09.200 --> 00:09:15.120
else could we see Luffy fight? The sky's the&nbsp;
limit, really. Perhaps he’ll have a rematch&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.120 --> 00:09:20.000
against one of the series’ first villains and&nbsp;
fellow Yonkou, Buggy the Clown. After all, at&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:20.000 --> 00:09:26.080
the rate that Buggy keeps failing upward, he might&nbsp;
be a true rival for the position of pirate king.

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:31.600
Maybe he’ll be forced into conflict with&nbsp;
a Marine that he has closer ties, too,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:38.320
since he is, after all, still a pirate. We’ve&nbsp;
built up a metric ton of hatred for Akainu,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:38.320 --> 00:09:46.000
but who wouldn’t be heartbroken seeing him have to&nbsp;
go all out against Coby, Smoker, or Grandpa Garp?

00:09:46.000 --> 00:09:48.880
After all, people have been sleeping on Coby,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.880 --> 00:09:55.280
future admiral - the secret final villain that&nbsp;
Oda has foreshadowed since Chapter 2 - his future&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:55.280 --> 00:10:01.680
power only makes sense given that he is a child&nbsp;
of Big Mom, as evidenced by his pink hair. Okay,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.680 --> 00:10:05.920
maybe I need to lay off the coffee. I might&nbsp;
be hitting these theories a little too hard.

00:10:07.600 --> 00:10:12.400
But the fight I am probably looking forward&nbsp;
the most right now, is in fact Shanks. And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:12.400 --> 00:10:17.520
if you want to understand, why this clash&nbsp;
between Shanks and Luffy is innevitable,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.520 --> 00:10:20.800
you should really not miss&nbsp;
out on this video right here.

